// Sandy Cove: a beach at low tide. The beacon stands halfway along a sandbar, a yard one tile
// wide and five long, so whoever holds it can be come at from either side. Sea-worn rocks stand
// either side of the bar between the starts, rather than in front of them, and the bar's two
// ends run out into the rocks.
// Every third turn a wave rolls over both ends of the sandbar and the sand beside them, washing
// whoever stands there toward the middle of the beach; a big shell on each side of the near
// edge, blown, calls the next wave in early.
id: cove
name: Sandy Cove
event: wash
event_name: wave
event_tiles: 3,1 4,1 5,1 3,5 4,5 5,5
event_first: 3
event_every: 3
switch_rest: 2
